INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "DOJ Internet Research Agency Indictment", "source_url": "https://www.justice.gov/d9/fieldable-panel-panes/basic-panes/attachments/2018/02/16/internet_research_agency_indictment.pdf", "text": "SRC-001: The indictment alleges that the Russian Internet Research Agency (IRA) operated from about 2014 to present to interfere with U.S. political and electoral processes, including the 2016 presidential election. It alleges funding by Yevgeniy Prigozhin and companies he controlled, Concord Management and Consulting and Concord Catering; Concord was the primary funding source. Project Lakhta's September 2016 monthly budget exceeded 73 million Russian rubles (over $1.25 million), with money concealed as software support/development and distributed through about 14 affiliate bank accounts. The IRA used false U.S. personas, stolen identities, social-media pages/groups posing as U.S.-controlled, targeted divisive U.S. political/social issues, bought ads in U.S. names, staged rallies, paid real U.S. persons, and contacted unwitting Trump-associated individuals/activists. It used U.S.-based infrastructure and false travel pretenses to hide Russian origin. Strategic goal: sow discord; by early/mid-2016 support Trump and disparage Hillary Clinton. It employed hundreds, had an annual budget in millions, and departments including graphics, data analysis, SEO, IT, finance. Translator project operated on YouTube, Facebook, Instagram, Twitter; by July 2016 more than 80 employees; stated goal included spreading distrust toward candidates and political system. The indictment is an allegation, not a conviction finding."}
